/target
/.serena
# Agent scaffolding: `.claude/worktrees/` holds the throwaway git worktrees
# that mutation-testing reviewers run in, so a reviewer breaking the tree on
# purpose cannot collide with an agent reading it. Created and removed per
# review; never project content.
/.claude
# Not committed (hiss convention): every CI/gate run re-resolves from the
# index, so a break inside a semver-compatible range surfaces immediately.
Cargo.lock
# The wire-v2 design record (rulings, frozen drafts, slice briefs, review
# evidence) — untracked by maintainer decision 2026-08-20. It stays on the
# maintainer's machine and in pre-removal git history; the crate never
# shipped it (Cargo.toml `exclude`). Consequence: worktree-isolated agents
# cannot see these files — a brief that needs ruling text must quote it.
/.slices
/.spec-v2-pipeline
/.spec-v2-clean-slate
